    <div class="lp-heading"><p class="lp-kicker">05 / Move the conversation forward</p><h2>How can cold calling accelerate<br>your LinkedIn lead generation?</h2><p>A relevant call can get you an answer while a message sits unread. Use the research to explain why you are calling, ask about the business and agree on a useful next step.</p></div>
    <div class="sg-flow"><div><h3>A good prospect has not replied.</h3><p>Call when the company fits and you have a reason to speak. Lead with the problem you can help solve. A connection acceptance alone does not prove buying interest.</p><p>Our <a href="/resources/linkedin-sales-navigator-lead-generation/">Sales Navigator vs Apollo guide</a> helps you choose the research and contact data for that first call.</p></div><div><h3>You need the right person.</h3><p>A company number can help you find who handles the issue when the contact is wrong or a mobile is missing. Confirm the person before sending another sequence.</p><p>Compare <a href="/resources/apollo-alternatives/">Apollo alternatives for phone data</a> and use our <a href="/resources/how-to-buy-cold-calling-leads/">mobile vs company number guide</a> to choose the route.</p></div><div><h3>An interested lead has gone quiet.</h3><p>A follow-up call can clarify timing, answer questions and turn interest into a meeting or a specific callback. Update the campaign after the conversation and honour stop requests across channels.</p><p>Keep ownership and follow-up in a <a href="/resources/best-crm-for-outbound-sales/">CRM built for outbound sales</a>.</p></div></div>
